Vikram and Betal: The Patient Student (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100141

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a student who wanted to learn many things,” said Betal. “But he wanted to learn everything very quickly.”

He often got frustrated when he could not understand something.

His teacher told him, “Learning takes time and patience.”

The student did not listen at first.

He kept rushing and made many mistakes.

Another student studied slowly and carefully.

Over time, the second student understood everything well.

Seeing this, the first student realized his mistake.

He started learning patiently.

Soon, he also became successful.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, what helped the student succeed?”

Vikram replied, “Patience and steady effort lead to success.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Patience is the key to learning.
